  Hello,

  This is Chu Yeow from Nitrous.IO. We incorrectly sent you an email a couple of days ago about your box *#{@box.name}* being due for termination. I'm very sorry for the mistake and rest assured that *#{@box.name}* will **not be terminated**.

  If you've any questions at all, you can contact me directly at [chuyeow@nitrous.io](mailto:chuyeow@nitrous.io) or via our general support inbox at [support@nitrous.io](mailto:support@nitrous.io).

  #### Why was there a mistake?

  We'd intended to notify users on our free tier that their boxes that **have not been used for more than 3 months** will be terminated soon. Unfortunately, there was an embarrassing bug where boxes that were **recently created** but **never logged in to** were also marked for termination.

  This has since been fixed and we will be more careful in future.

  #### What exactly is the Nitrous.IO box termination policy?

  Some of you have shared with us that you think 5 days is too short of a notice to terminate free boxes. This is a one-time event; we'll be giving significantly more notice in the future before terminating free boxes.

  We should note that while there is no obligation to upgrade to a paid plan (we love all our users!), boxes *never terminate* on [paid plans](https://www.nitrous.io/pricing).

  Sincerely,<br>
  Chu Yeow from Nitrous.IO
